              "ev-16c1f18c99c2-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 1,
              "start": 1
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The petitioners are the Lac du Flambeau Band of Lake Superior Chippewa Indians."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f35ba1fba948c11f3ad69786f6fc6a27e627789845690d6513f9ce8e12c12f61",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f35ba1fba948-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Brian W. Coughlin, the respondent, fled a motion in Bankruptcy Court seeking to enforce the automatic stay and recover damages."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "16c1f18c99c2c0b3a88a0bf1216fa02155038bf827c4c52533436d86e0f9e5c7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-16c1f18c99c2-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners, petitioners allege that after filing for bankruptcy, the creditor continued to contact Coughlin, leading to a suicide attempt."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "16c1f18c99c2c0b3a88a0bf1216fa02155038bf827c4c52533436d86e0f9e5c7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-16c1f18c99c2-0000-0003",
              "ev-16c1f18c99c2-0001-0000",
              "ev-16c1f18c99c2-0001-0001",
              "ev-16c1f18c99c2-0001-0003",
              "ev-16c1f18c99c2-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The central legal question is whether the phrase \u201cother foreign or domestic government\u201d in the Bankruptcy Code\u2019s sovereign\u2011immunity waiver includes Indian tribes."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Background and Question",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "case_id": "2022-22-227",
  "decision": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f35ba1fba948c11f3ad69786f6fc6a27e627789845690d6513f9ce8e12c12f61",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f35ba1fba948-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 13,
              "start": 13
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The majority held that the Bankruptcy Code\u2019s \u00a7\u202f106(a) unequivocally abrogates sovereign immunity of all governments, and because tribes are governments, it also abrogates tribal sovereign immunity."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f35ba1fba948c11f3ad69786f6fc6a27e627789845690d6513f9ce8e12c12f61",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f35ba1fba948-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 19,
              "start": 19
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Thomas, in a concurrence, agreed that the statutory provisions extend to all governments and declined to read any ambiguity into the language."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Decision",
    "status": "complete",
